1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,352
I bought three extra hours of life today, and the price was my first kiss.

2
00:00:05,652 --> 00:00:14,340
The time broker smiled, sliding a glowing glass marble across the metal desk. My chest felt instantly lighter.

3
00:00:14,640 --> 00:00:21,840
Everyone in this city trades their past to cheat the clock. A childhood pet for a Tuesday afternoon.

4
00:00:22,140 --> 00:00:28,620
A college graduation for a quiet Sunday morning. We are all dying to live, by forgetting how.

5
00:00:28,920 --> 00:00:36,000
Tonight, I needed a whole week. To finish the painting that would finally make me immortal.

6
00:00:36,300 --> 00:00:43,020
The broker didn't want memories of my youth this time. He wanted something much heavier.

7
00:00:43,320 --> 00:00:51,648
He wanted the day I turn thirty. The entire day. My absolute peak. I signed the contract without blinking.

8
00:00:51,948 --> 00:01:00,948
Instantly, my mind violently lurched forward. I bypassed my thirtieth birthday entirely, landing right after it.

9
00:01:01,248 --> 00:01:08,616
The painting on my easel was finished. A masterpiece. But my hands were old, trembling, and frail.

10
00:01:08,916 --> 00:01:15,756
I never lived the day I became great. If tomorrow is already gone, what are you waiting for today?
